ZONE SIMULATOR
Complete User Guide
________________________________________
Part 1 – Introduction
1.1 Overview
Zone Simulator is a tool designed to manage hydraulic connectivity between pressure zones in a water distribution network.
In zoned systems (e.g., pressure zones, district metered areas), pipes that connect one zone to another are classified as boundary pipes. These pipes determine whether water can flow between adjacent zones.
The purpose of this application is to allow engineers to determine which boundary pipes remain:
•	Open – allowing hydraulic flow between zones
•	Closed – isolating zones from one another
The system provides both automatic rule-based selection and manual interactive control.
________________________________________
1.2 Visual Representation
The network is displayed using standardized color coding:
Visual Element	Meaning
Dark blue thin lines	Regular pipes (not boundaries)
Green thick lines	Open boundary pipes
Red thick lines	Closed boundary pipes
Blue thick lines	Hovered pipe
Pink dashed lines	Filtered/highlighted elements
Colored polygons	Pressure zones
Gold dots	Flow direction animation
Colored nodes	Attribute-based colormap
