Outside Zones	Nodes not assigned to zones
________________________________________
4.2 Boundary Strategy Settings
4.2.1 Include Boundaries with Unassigned Areas
•	Unchecked (default): Only Zone↔Zone pipes count
•	Checked: Zone↔Outside pipes included
Use when analyzing full network connectivity.
________________________________________
4.2.2 Show Zone Boundaries on Map
Displays colored zone polygons.
Recommended for:
•	Presentations
•	Learning zone layout
Disable for clearer pipe visualization.
________________________________________
4.2.3 Hide Closed Boundaries
•	Unchecked: Show open and closed boundaries
•	Checked: Show only open boundaries
Useful for reducing visual clutter.
________________________________________
4.2.4 Reset Before Applying
•	Checked: Close all boundaries before applying new rules
•	Unchecked: Add new selections to existing configuration
________________________________________
4.3 Connection Management
4.3.1 Open Connections per Zone Pair
Defines number of open pipes between each zone pair.
Value	Meaning
0	Complete isolation
1	Single connection
2+	Redundant connections
Important: Applied per zone pair.
________________________________________
4.3.2 Link Type Filters
Users may include or exclude:
•	Pipes
•	Pumps
•	Valves
This allows targeted analysis.
________________________________________
4.3.3 Prioritization Attribute
Users select a numeric attribute such as:
•	Diameter
•	Length
•	Flowrate
•	Velocity
•	Headloss
•	Roughness
________________________________________
4.3.4 Highest vs. Lowest Selection
•	Highest: Selects largest attribute values
•	Lowest: Selects smallest attribute values
Example: If prioritizing diameter and selecting Highest, the largest diameter pipes remain open.
________________________________________
